// waiver: the conferral's two-sentence oracle phrasing ("Each Vampire creature
// card you own that isn't on the battlefield has madness. The madness cost is
// equal to its mana cost.") is beyond the renderer. The `Each(SelectAll(..),
// GainAbility(Keyword(Madness(ManaCostOf(..)))))` grant renders as the bare
// anthem "All creatures have madness." — the renderer drops the complex
// SelectAll scope (Vampire ∧ owned-by-you ∧ off-battlefield) to "All", omits
// the `ManaCostOf` madness cost, and has no second cost sentence.
//
// The card static below is the FAITHFUL model of the printed ability and is
// what renders on the card. Its FUNCTIONAL half — the madness self-replacement
// actually firing when an owned off-battlefield Vampire is discarded — rides a
// companion `rules/grant/` ConferralRule (`falkenrath-gorger-madness.ron`): the
// engine gathers conditionally-conferred replacement/triggered abilities from
// predicate-scoped ConferralRules (`derive::derived_abilities_of`), not from a
// layer-view `GainAbility` grant, so the grant alone would render but never
// open the [CR#616.1] discard window. The ConferralRule scope is unconditional
// (no "you own" / "a Gorger is on the battlefield" gate — a ConferralRule has
// no source object to anchor "you", and a `Where(..)` scope has no carrier so
// it can't reference Gorger); this is the conferral machinery's documented
// global-rule limitation, acceptable for canon madness coverage.
Normal(
  name: "Falkenrath Gorger",
  mana_cost: [
    Red,
  ],
  types: [
    Creature,
  ],
  subtypes: [
    Vampire,
    Berserker,
  ],
  abilities: [
    Static(Each(
      SelectAll(And([Creature, Subtype("Vampire"), Owner(Ref(You)), Not(InZone(Battlefield))])),
      Modify(It, GainAbility(Keyword(Madness([ManaCostOf(It)])))),
    )),
  ],
  power: 2,
  toughness: 1,
)
